And cell phones back when I was in high school were not popular, not everyone had one, but she had one lent from her mom just in case anything, anything happened if she had to make any phone calls. And it was a, you know, a kind of brick of a phone as the old ones were. And she holds it up and she says to this guy, I've got a cell phone and I'll call the cops. And so this doesn't sink in right away to the guy who keeps on slapping me and threatening

